==== verdict ====
GATE B (SAMPLED Probe B rel_err/cos_move) is the fidelity arbiter for EVERY
'did it help' call below. Probe C (teacher-forced x0_relerr) is GATE A: a MATH
wiring check only, read differently per parameterization:
  [eps-param] Probe C x0_relerr RISES with t (1/sqrt(acp) amplification, intrinsic);
    low-t eps_mse~0 but mid/high-t x0 poor => amplification, not necessarily a bug.
    x0_relerr large even at LOW t => schedule/inversion BUG (fix before training).
A good + B bad  => phase/sliding-condition issue (rebuild dataset, retrain).
A ~= B-success >> B-failed => eval-set CONTAMINATION (H8): the probe/eval mix
    ~34-37% FAILED demos the success-trained GDM rightly mispredicts.
    Fix the EVAL episode set (--eval-filter success20), not the model.
A and B bad     => capacity/undertraining (train longer / more data).
collapse << 1   => model predicts ~mean subgoal regardless of input.
